# Code owners for the merge-admission gate.
#
# A pull request's own copy of a workflow file is what GitHub runs on that pull
# request, so a candidate could rewrite the gate that admits it. The durable fix,
# an organization ruleset requiring the workflow from main, needs GitHub Team;
# ZK-Theory is on Free. Decided by Stephen on 2026-09-11: these files are owned
# here, and P-049 requires code-owner review. Changes to the gate therefore need
# a deliberate admin bypass, which GitHub records in rule insights.
#
# Takes effect only once "Require review from Code Owners" is enabled in the
# P-049 ruleset. tests/tools/test_ci_platform_policy.py keeps this list aligned
# with the files the gate actually depends on.

/.github/CODEOWNERS                              @stephendor
/.github/merge-admission.yml                     @stephendor
/.github/workflows/merge-admission.yml           @stephendor
/.github/workflows/merge-admission-sweep.yml     @stephendor
/.github/workflows/ci.yml                        @stephendor
/tools/check_merge_admission.py                  @stephendor
